  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$(6y+3)(6y-3)=$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=6y$ and $b=3,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6y+3)(6y-3) & = \\\\ (6y)^{2}-{3}^{2} & = \\\\ 36{y}^{2}-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
